{
  "_README": [
    "TEMPLATE 3 of 4 — REPEATABLE SERVICE PAGE  (/services/data-destruction)",
    "",
    "This is the pattern for all 7 service pages. To adapt it, change only: the Service node,",
    "the ImageObject, the WebPage node, the breadcrumb leaf, and the FAQ. Everything else is",
    "byte-identical across pages.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS FIXES vs your live markup",
    "  1. provider was a 4-property stub pointing at an @id defined only on the homepage.",
    "     Google does not resolve @id across pages, so this page had NO business entity — no",
    "     address, no geo, no hours — while trying to rank for 'data destruction Cincinnati'.",
    "  2. areaServed was a flat array of plain strings ('Cincinnati, Ohio'). Strings are legal",
    "     but create no place entities. Typed City/State/AdministrativeArea nodes plus a",
    "     GeoCircle do.",
    "  3. No WebPage node at all. Your healthcare page has one; this one does not.",
    "  4. No image. The page has a hero at data-destruction-service-hero.png that nothing",
    "     declared, and og:image points at the logo.",
    "  5. No serviceOutput, no compliance properties, no offers, no availableChannel.",
    "",
    "RICH RESULT ELIGIBILITY",
    "  Breadcrumbs — live today.",
    "  Video — once you add the video you mentioned. The VideoObject node below is ready; fill",
    "    it in and delete it until then. This is the single biggest rich-result win available",
    "    on this page.",
    "  Service itself is NOT a rich result type. It is still worth marking up: it is what makes",
    "    the page machine-readable for AI surfaces and entity comprehension.",
    "",
    "Strip all _README and _comment keys before shipping."
  ],

